core

# --- SALP ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Real GACPD runs carry whole source trees; external tools are large,
# platform-specific binaries. Both are kept locally, never committed.
data/gacpd/*
!data/gacpd/.gitkeep
!data/gacpd/README.md

data/repos/*
!data/repos/.gitkeep
!data/repos/README.md

tools/**
!tools/README.md
!tools/*/
!tools/*/.gitkeep

# Pipeline output
/out/
data/out/
.refactoring-cache/

# RefactoringMiner unzips a GitHub source archive into <cwd>/<project>-<sha>/
# when it is given a commit the local clone does not contain. `salp run` guards
# against reaching that path at all (see analyzers/tools.py), but a stray manual
# invocation should not show up as hundreds of megabytes of untracked files.
/*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*
data/*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*
